\ ***************************************************************************
\ The keyboard, read straight from the System VIA, as Chuckie Egg 2's port
\ does: the game makes no OS calls.
\ ***************************************************************************

\ Is a key down? X = its internal key number. NZ if it is.
.key_down
    LDA #&7F : STA sysvia_ddra      ; bits 0-6 the key, bit 7 its state
    LDA #3 : STA sysvia_orb         ; auto-scan off: the matrix is ours
    STX sysvia_ora_nh
    LDA sysvia_ora_nh : AND #&80
    RTS

\ BBC internal key numbers
K_SHIFT  = &00
K_Q      = &10
K_P      = &37
K_SPACE  = &62
K_RETURN = &49
K_A      = &41
K_Z      = &61
K_X      = &42
K_C      = &52
K_F      = &43
K_G      = &53
K_COMMA  = &66
K_STOP   = &67
K_SLASH  = &68
K_SEMI   = &57
K_COLON  = &48

\ The players' controls (decision 13): magic, up, down, right, left, fire.
\ Chosen for a laptop's keyboard in an emulator, where jsbeeb puts each of
\ these BBC keys on the laptop's key in the same place: player 1 Z and X
\ left and right, C down, F up, G fire and A magic; player 2 the same
\ shape on the right, with , . / ; RETURN, and : (a laptop's ') magic.
.controls
    EQUB K_A, K_F, K_C, K_X, K_Z, K_G
    EQUB K_COLON, K_SEMI, K_SLASH, K_STOP, K_COMMA, K_RETURN
